{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall not pervert the justice of a stranger or an orphan.</b> As for the rich, he was already warned ״לֹא תַטֶּה מִשְׁפָּט״ (Deuteronomy 16), and He repeated concerning the poor to transgress on it with two prohibitions, because it is easy to pervert the justice of a poor person more than that of a rich man — therefore He warned and repeated concerning it (Sifrei)." "<b>And you shall not take a pledge.</b> Not at the time of the loan."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:16.426137957Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}